    "updated_at": "2025-03-20T17:33:07Z",
    "body": "It seems to me that for the remaining state override cases (path start state, opaque path state, query state, and fragment state) it should not check the return value at all. (I suppose it could assert the return value is not failure, but I'm not sure if that's better from just not looking at it which is what we do for the `URL` API.)",
