    "updated_at": "2025-03-20T21:11:08Z",
    "body": "WebKit does not treat those as errors currently. I wrote these tests to verify:\n```json\n  {\n    \"pattern\": [{ \"port\": \"80\" }],\n    \"inputs\": [{ \"port\": \"8\\t0\" }],\n    \"expected_match\": {\n      \"port\": { \"input\": \"80\", \"groups\": {}}\n    }\n  },  \n  {\n    \"pattern\": [{ \"port\": \"80\" }],\n    \"inputs\": [{ \"port\": \"80x\" }],\n    \"expected_match\": {\n      \"port\": { \"input\": \"80\", \"groups\": {}}\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"pattern\": [{ \"port\": \"80\" }],\n    \"inputs\": [{ \"port\": \"80?x\" }],\n    \"expected_match\": {\n      \"port\": { \"input\": \"80\", \"groups\": {}}\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"pattern\": [{ \"port\": \"80\" }],\n    \"inputs\": [{ \"port\": \"80\\\\x\" }],\n    \"expected_match\": {\n      \"port\": { \"input\": \"80\", \"groups\": {}}\n    }\n  },\n```\nWhich would be more consistent with how the hostname override works so let me prepare a patch against the URL standard that aligns with this.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
